al guess toward truth rather than an expectation of future success"}, {"block": "45a1f718f1ba5cef95d17a00cd3e8bf3110234c845cf9afb34610eeb68868559", "quote": "A theory with higher empirical content has survived more severe tests, making it a better candidate for being close to the truth (verisimilitude), even if its logical probability remains low or undefined."}], "successor_question": "Can a non-inductive criterion be given that distinguishes using corroboration to rank theories by truth-likeness from using corroboration to rank theories by expected future performance — or are these the same inference under different labels?", "counterexample": null}